+# Redis Quota Economics — Decision Memo + Command-Shaping Audit (#1732 / R28)
+
+- **Probe dates**: tower chain telemetry 2026-10-30T01:45Z (live `redis_rotation_status`/`redis_stats`);
+  Upstash pricing page 2026-10-30; Valkey release index 2026-10-30 (GitHub API). Every price and
+  usage figure below carries its probe date — re-probe before deciding.
+- **Lane**: docs-only, zero source changes, zero new dependencies, `.github/` untouched (per #1732).
+- **Task ID**: bridge-20261028-scout-radar-viii (verdict `adapt_cleanroom`).
+
+## 1. Decision table (maintainer can decide from this row alone)
+
+| Option | Price (probed 2026-10-30) | Command ceiling | Fits the chain? | Verdict |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| **Stay free (status quo)** | $0 — 5 accounts × 1 DB each × 500K cmds/mo (free tier = 1 database per free account) | 2,500,000/mo chain total | Yes — current architecture | **Recommended now** (see §2: observed burn makes exhaustion a non-event) |
+| **PAYG** | $0.20 per 100K commands (unlimited) | Unlimited | Yes — same client, flip a flag | Elastic middle; at current burn would cost ≈ **$0.04/mo** (≈18K cmds/mo) — the meter, not the money, is the point |
+| **Fixed 250MB** | $10/mo (+$5 per read region) | **Unlimited commands**, 10K cmd/s | Yes — kills the quota problem class entirely | The availability kill-switch if burn ever grows ~100×; also removes the entire rotation registry's reason to exist |
+| **Valkey self-host** | License BSD-3-Clause; latest stable **9.1.3** (published 2026-10-26) | Hardware-bound, no vendor quota | No — new ops surface (hosting, persistence, backups, HA) | Escape hatch only; explicitly out of this lane (#1732 never-do) |
+
+Billing fine print (Upstash docs, probed 2026-10-30): `pipeline`/`MULTI` are billed **per command**
+(MULTI/EXEC = N+2; `EVAL` = 1 + every internal `redis.call`); `INFO`/`PING`/`CONFIG`/`COMMAND` are
+**unbilled** — the tower's polling lane already rides the free class. REST `/pipeline` saves HTTP
+round-trips, **not** billable commands.
+
+## 2. Quota-burn horizon (live math, probed 2026-10-30T01:45Z)
+
+Chain state at probe: `primary` 480,000/500,000 (soft-threshold hit, cooldown until reset);
+`secondary` 480,000/500,000 (same); **`tertiary` ACTIVE at 1,314/500,000**; `quaternary` 21;
+`quinary` 21 (fifth account, added since #1732 was filed — chain is now 5 wide, not 4).
+`nextGlobalResetAt` **2026-11-01T00:01Z** (~22h after probe).
+
+- Observed active-primary burn: 92 → 1,314 between filing (2026-10-28) and probe = **~600 cmds/day**.
+- Exhaustion horizon on the active account at that rate: ≈ **830 days** — the "#1698 outage horizon
+  stays real" premise is **no longer time-urgent**; the monthly reset makes it structurally moot.
+- Historical context: primary+secondary sat at 480K over ~28 days of the pre-rotation era
+  (≈17K cmds/day implied). Post-rotation observed burn (~600/day) is ≈ **28× lower** — the #646
+  debounces (heartbeat/presence 60s), the 5s L1 read-through cache, and the mirror-served read
+  pattern did the actual quota saving. **Rotation itself buys availability, not quota** — total
+  budget is 5 × 500K regardless of order — and that statement remains true as filed.
+- Decision guidance: stay free while burn ≪ chain budget (today: 0.7%/mo utilization at observed
+  rate). If any month's chain burn exceeds ~50% (1.25M) or the burn rate grows ~100×, pick
+  Fixed $10 — it deletes the quota class instead of managing it.
+
